Z||000010||Supernaut||08-06-2000||03:47 PM||||Just finished going over the new car in detail.  I am very pleased with it, the only things I can find wrong are a headliner that is starting to come loose in a couple of corners and a possible EGR tube problem.  It runs great...smooth and strong.<P>It is amazing to sit in a car that is 14 years old that still looks (and if I try hard enough, smells) like a new one. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I have warned the kids not to even look at it!  Have set up a safe perimeter in the garage that no bicycle may enter LOL.<P>I've owned that old Jimmy since it was new and it was a good truck...in 10 years all I ever had to replace was the alternator (twice), the fuel pump and the O2 sensor. Filters, plugs and gas will keep a 4.3 happy and dependable.  But it was definitely feeling the miles...better to make this deal than to have my wife stranded on the freeway at 3am after something finally gives out.<P>Still have a big 'ol suburban to get around in the snow and carry the kidsaround in when needed, but now the wife and I can start attending Fiero gatherings in a fiero!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm going to go take her around the loop now.<P><P>------------------<BR>Supernaut<BR>86 GT (in progress)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/signat.gif"> ||||reg||12
